{"timestamp":"2026-08-27T09:28:43.090Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0428c-dd52-7501-baf0-fa958f05d545","call_id":"call_ePRcmYHq7ewXdkU3XseflxJx","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"# Compression Benchmarks\n\nThis directory contains GPU compression and ATS/direct-host-access benchmarks\nfor BF16 KV blocks and model weights.\n\nThe C++/CUDA binaries focus on nvCOMP Bitcomp host-compression paths.  The\nPython benchmarks compare H2D+decompress, ATS-direct decompression, ZipServ,\nDietGPU, and CPU zstd mantissa decompression paths.\n\nRun commands from the repository root:\n\n```bash\ncd /root/projects/ats-benchmarks\n```\n\nUse the `tiered-serve` Python environment for Python benchmarks:\n\n```bash\nPY=/root/projects/tiered-serve/.venv/bin/python\n```\n\n## Build\n\nBuild the compression binaries:\n\n```bash\nmake bitcomp\nmake bitcomp_omp\n```\n\nOr build every compression binary:\n\n```bash\nmake compress\n```\n\nThe Python benchmarks JIT-build their required PyTorch CUDA extensions on first\nrun.  They expect the sibling repositories and libraries referenced by the\nscripts to be available, including `tiered-serve`, `LLM-bitfield-compressor`,\nCUDA, nvCOMP, and DietGPU/ZipServ dependencies for the selected codec.\n\n## Native Bitcomp Benchmarks\n\nSingle-path Bitcomp benchmark:\n\n```bash\n./bin/bitcomp --chunks 8192 --chunk-bytes 32768 --iters 1 --verify 1\n```\n\nOpenMP copy-vs-ATS Bitcomp benchmark:\n\n```bash\n./bin/bitcomp_omp \\\n  --chunks 8192 \\\n  --chunk-bytes 32768 \\\n  --pattern random \\\n  --iters 1 \\\n  --verify 1\n```\n\nOptional OpenMP thread pinning:\n\n```bash\nexport OMP_NUM_THREADS=16\nexport OMP_DYNAMIC=false\nexport OMP_PROC_BIND=true\nexport OMP_PLACES=cores\n```\n\n## nvCOMP H2D vs ATS\n\n`python/nvcomp_h2d_vs_ats.py` compares compressed BF16 data copied to HBM before\ndecompression against compressed data read directly from registered hugepage host\nmemory through ATS.  It also reports SM-copy bandwidth from host memory to HBM.\n\n```bash\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/nvcomp_h2d_vs_ats.py\n\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/nvcomp_h2d_vs_ats.py \\\n  --codec ans bitcomp zipserv \\\n  --size-mib 64\n\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/nvcomp_h2d_vs_ats.py \\\n  --codec all \\\n  --block-sweep 1 16 256 4096\n\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/nvcomp_h2d_vs_ats.py \\\n  --codec zipserv \\\n  --use-kv-cache\n```\n\nSupported codecs are `gdeflate`, `zstd`, `bitcomp`, `lz4`, `ans`, and\n`zipserv`.  The default generated block shape is `128x128` BF16, or 32 KiB per\nblock.\n\n## BF16 Split Exp/Sign-Mantissa ATS\n\n`python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py` benchmarks split-stream BF16\nreconstruct/decompress latency with compressed exponent and sign-mantissa\nstreams placed in HBM or LPDDR/ATS-backed hugepage memory.  It supports\ngenerated BF16 blocks, `kv_blocks_cache.pt` inputs, and `.safetensors` or `.pt`\nweight inputs.  It prints HBM, Exp-in-ATS, and Exp+sign_mantissa-in-ATS rows.\n\nGenerated data:\n\n```bash\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py \\\n  --codec dietgpu \\\n  --size-mib 256\n\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py \\\n  --codec zipserv \\\n  --size-mib 256\n\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py \\\n  --codec all \\\n  --size-mib 256\n```\n\nFile inputs:\n\n```bash\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py \\\n  benchmarks/compress/kv_blocks_cache.pt \\\n  --codec all \\\n  --max-tensors 256\n\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py \\\n  /path/to/model-00001-of-00030.safetensors \\\n  --codec all \\\n  --layer 0 \\\n  --max-tensors 128\n```\n\nOptional placement sanity check:\n\n```bash\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py \\\n  benchmarks/compress/kv_blocks_cache.pt \\\n  --codec zipserv \\\n  --max-tensors 4096 \\\n  --measure-exp-copy\n```\n\n`Write GB/s` is decompressed BF16 output write throughput.  `Read GB/s` counts\nthe compressed/reconstruct input streams read by the timed path.  `LPDDR GB/s`\ncounts only the streams placed in LPDDR for that row: Exp for the `Exp` row,\nand Exp+sign_mantissa for the `Exp+SM` row.  If HBM and ATS decompress latency\nare close, use `--measure-exp-copy` to measure the Exp stream by itself and\nconfirm the HBM-vs-ATS bandwidth gap.\n\nFor ZipServ, the default `--zipserv-api pure` path precomputes output pointers\nand `start_exp` on GPU before timing, so the measured HBM row does not include\nthe legacy binding's per-call control H2D copies.  Use `--zipserv-api legacy`\nonly when intentionally timing the original Python binding path.\n\nFor DietGPU, the default `--dietgpu-api pure` path precomputes pointer and\ncapacity arrays on GPU before timing, so the measured HBM row does not include\nDietGPU's per-call pointer-array H2D copies.  `--dietgpu-api inline128` is a\nfallback that avoids those copies by using DietGPU's <=128-block inline-provider\npath, and `--dietgpu-api legacy` times the original single-call binding.\n\n## zstd Mantissa ATS\n\n`python/zstd_mantissa_ats.py` compresses BF16 mantissa tiles with zstd, then\ncompares CPU decompression through a DMA path against CPU direct C2C access to\nGPU HBM on GH200-style systems.\n\n```bash\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/zstd_mantissa_ats.py \\\n  /path/to/model-00001-of-00030.safetensors\n\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/zstd_mantissa_ats.py \\\n  /path/to/model-00001-of-00030.safetensors \\\n  --tile 512 \\\n  --workers 64 \\\n  --layer 0 \\\n  --max-weights 7\n\n$PY benchmarks/compress/python/zstd_mantissa_ats.py \\\n  /path/to/model.pt \\\n  --all-weights \\\n  --max-weights 16\n```\n\n## ATS and Hugepages\n\nThe ATS benchmarks use hugepage-backed host memory by default:\n\n```bash\n--hugepage-dir /mnt/hugepages\n```\n\nMake sure that directory is mounted and has enough free hugepage capacity for\nthe selected data size.  Use smaller `--size-mib`, `--num-blocks`, or\n`--max-tensors` values when doing quick smoke tests or when hugepage memory is\nlimited.\n## main...origin/main\n M benchmarks/compress/python/bf16_split_decompress_ats.py\n M benchmarks/compress/python/nvcomp_h2d_vs_ats.py\n?? benchmarks/compress/bench_cpu_encode_compare.py\n?? benchmarks/compress/bench_kv_compress_latency.py\n?? benchmarks/compress/bench_p4flat_kv.py\n?? benchmarks/compress/bench_p4flat_kv_threads.py\n?? benchmarks/compress/kv_blocks_cache.pt\n?? benchmarks/compress/test_p4flat_cpp_encode.py\n?? cpu_hbm_test.py\na6d522b Add mantissa exp split benchmark\n92938fa Add benchmark for zstd\ndeb78e8 Add compression benchmark\n8465864 Add embedding benchmark\n309ab1a Fix makefile\n32e93d8 Initial commit\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04287-0fd9-7860-86ed-0dfd530834d8","create_time":1787822923.0906873}}}
